<FeatureFacts id="plugins" />

Plugins add widgets, progression rules, nutrition targets, analytics and exercise or mobility packs.
Code plugins run in a sandbox with no access to the network or the rest of your data. See
[Trust & the sandbox](/docs/plugins/trust).

<HowTo id="pro.plugins" />

## For coaches

<FeatureFacts id="coach-plugins" />

Coaching › Plugins shows the kinds you use with clients: progression rules, nutrition targets,
workout blocks, and exercise, program, meal plan, recipe and card packs. **Installed** is what you
have; **Community** is the directory. Plugins that run code are marked *Runs code*: clients are
asked to allow them before they run on their phone. Packs are data, so there's nothing to install:
program packs open in Programs › Start from a program, and meal plan and recipe packs in Nutrition,
where **Copy to yours** makes your own copy (a newer pack never changes it).

A plugin's panel says what it's given and what it can do, **Used in** (which of your programs use a
block or rule) and how many clients allowed it. Uninstalling something a program uses warns you
first: those blocks turn into plain notes clients log by hand.

**Card packs** add cards to your Today and Your month (Edit cards › Add a card). They only see
your roster: first names, months with you, check-ins waiting, and sessions and program week for
clients who share workouts. Never payments, messages, food, weight or photos.

## Build your own

<FeatureFacts id="plugin-builder" />

For the details of each plugin type, see [Building plugins](/docs/plugins).

